 "notes": [
  "SPLENDOUR (client/scenes/court/wardrobe_view.gd), on the painted pages' host (PaintedPage). `page` is the whole painting. Its stretch band is the grid's erased ground (rows 470..1250, the same all the way down between the frame's sides), so a taller canvas shows more tiles; `ground` is the blurred surround's colour at the top, carried up behind the notch.",
  "tabs: the game's one tab strip (TabStrip) in the painted row's place: its plates are narrower than the painting's (tabs_sheet_b), so the strip's rect is centred on the row (y 412) and its floor is the plates' foot.",
  "grid: tiles of `tile` in three columns at pitch 284 x 270 from (50, 461) -- 3 x 272 + 2 x 12 across the painting's 50..890 -- inside a scroll, as many rows as the tab holds. A tile's frame (frames/<art>_tile), crest (drawn down to the box), title (on the scroll) or colour (icons/colour_chip with its face tinted, as the Royal Store draws one) is centred in `art`; `name` is on the painted plate, with `hint` under it for a locked one.",
  "strip: the lord as the realm sees them: their face in the frame they wear, their name in their colour, their title on the scroll, their colour's chip and their crest.",
  "equip: the painted plate with its word set in type (EQUIP's ink is 40 tall): EQUIP, TAKE OFF, the price, or LOCKED."
 ],
